### What happened?

Requesting `gemini-3-pro-preview` with `--model` returns a response from **`gemini-3.1-pro-preview`** (or fails with quota limits for `gemini-3.1-pro`) whenever the Gemini 3.1 rollout is active (`useGemini3_1: true`).

The CLI silently overrides the user's explicit model version without any warning or notification.

This is the exact Pro-tier analogue to #28859 (which fixed silent remapping for Flash models in #29252). While PR #29252 prevented explicit Flash model versions from being silently upgraded, explicit Pro preview models are still intercepted by fallthrough and resolution context rules.

#### Repro

```bash
gemini --prompt "say ok" --model gemini-3-pro-preview --skip-trust --output-format json
```

#### Actual Behavior

The request is rewritten and dispatched to `gemini-3.1-pro-preview` (or fails with `Quota exceeded ... model: gemini-3.1-pro`).

#### Root Cause

1. In `packages/core/src/config/models.ts`:
```typescript
